# Deploy target: ck6filter

Going forward, ship product changes to the **ck6filter@cavinkare.com** stack:

- **GitHub:** `https://github.com/6Filter/6-Filter-Test.git` (remote `origin`, branch `main`)
- **Render account / workspace:** logged in as `ck6filter@cavinkare.com` (`tea-dbta5et6e07s73bsi9t0`)
- **Web service:** `ck-6-filter-test` (`srv-dbtckp67bikc73dnujvg`) → https://ck-6-filter-test-88wu.onrender.com
- **Postgres:** `6-Filter-Test-Live` (`dpg-dbtca9rbc2fs73doghpg-a`)

## Workflow after meaningful code changes

1. Commit (when the user asks, or when they asked to push/deploy).
2. `git push origin HEAD` (pre-push runs `ciDryRun`; fix real failures, do not `--no-verify`).
3. Ensure Render `ck-6-filter-test` is linked to `https://github.com/6Filter/6-Filter-Test` on `main` with:
   - `buildCommand`: `npm ci --include=dev && npm run build`
   - `startCommand`: `npm start`
   - `autoDeployTrigger`: `commit`
4. If auto-deploy does not fire, `render deploys create srv-dbtckp67bikc73dnujvg --confirm`.

## Blocker to remember

If Render returns `repository URL is invalid or unfetchable`, the **ck6filter** Render account has not connected the GitHub App to the private `6Filter` org. Ask the user to open Render → Account Settings → GitHub → Connect / Configure → grant `6Filter`, then retry the service repo PATCH + deploy. Do not leave the service on `render-examples/express-hello-world`.

Do not print Render API keys or database URLs.
